1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,800
So, let's start a discussion with IO device, IO devices are nothing but interfaces with

2
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:17,680
which a computer can communicate with a user and a user can communicate with a computer.

3
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:25,360
If a user wants to command a computer to do something or it wants to get the result from

4
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:35,800
the computer, it can do that using these interfaces like IO devices and IO devices as the name

5
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:43,240
suggests like I here is input, O here is output. So, there are two devices, two types of devices,

6
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:48,320
input devices and output devices. Now, input devices are nothing but the devices that are

7
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:58,520
capable of receiving the data from whom from user and providing this data to whom computer

8
00:00:58,520 --> 00:00:59,520
ok.

9
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:08,750
So, input devices are nothing but something that is take input or receive something like

10
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:14,110
data from user ok.

11
00:01:14,110 --> 00:01:21,470
And it gives this data to whom to processing unit but again let us consider it to be computer

12
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:26,950
ok CPU processing unit ok.

13
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:28,790
This is input device ok.

14
00:01:28,790 --> 00:01:30,710
So what is output device?

15
00:01:30,710 --> 00:01:33,870
Output device is kind of the opposite of this.

16
00:01:33,870 --> 00:01:42,430
So output device is nothing but a device that are capable of receiving the data from a computer

17
00:01:42,430 --> 00:01:52,150
or processing unit of a computer and providing it to user.

18
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:54,510
What is the block diagram for this?

19
00:01:54,510 --> 00:02:04,160
There is a computer here, it will be receiving data from CPU, processing unit of computer

20
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:12,330
and it will be giving or providing this data to user.

21
00:02:12,330 --> 00:02:17,610
So, for example, like input device, what all things are input device, keyboard is an input

22
00:02:17,610 --> 00:02:23,650
device, optical pen is an input device, scanner, barcode reader, joystick, all these things

23
00:02:23,650 --> 00:02:25,650
are input devices.

24
00:02:25,650 --> 00:02:33,170
Whereas headset, headphone, screen, monitor, monitor is a big part right, I think monitor

25
00:02:33,170 --> 00:02:34,170
everyone uses.

26
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:41,490
So, monitor is an output device, laser printer, inkjet printer, speaker, all these things

27
00:02:41,490 --> 00:02:55,470
are output devices. Let me ask you one thing, is pendrive an input device or an output device?

28
00:02:55,470 --> 00:03:03,670
So I think you must have seen it here, it is input device as well as output device.

29
00:03:03,670 --> 00:03:05,950
But how is that?

30
00:03:05,950 --> 00:03:10,750
How is it input device as well as output device?

31
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:19,430
So for example, you have a friend and whenever you go to your friend's house to get this

32
00:03:19,430 --> 00:03:24,550
movie in your pendrive, so what is this pendrive now?

33
00:03:24,550 --> 00:03:32,070
This pendrive acts as an output device, since it receives like it receives the data from

34
00:03:32,070 --> 00:03:38,790
your friends computer, the data that is saved in your friends computer, you are receiving

35
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:44,430
that information in this device, in this pen drive, that is why it is an output device.

36
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:53,150
Whereas, when you come home and plug this pen drive into your computer, then it becomes

37
00:03:53,150 --> 00:03:54,830
an input device.

38
00:03:54,830 --> 00:04:00,230
So, therefore, basically storage units are both input device and output device, whatever

39
00:04:00,230 --> 00:04:08,310
we store during the storage like while writing it is input device, it is output device and

40
00:04:08,310 --> 00:04:17,510
whenever we are fetching like reading it is kind of input device, okay.

41
00:04:17,510 --> 00:04:24,310
So now this input device and output device are actually very very important for us, why?

42
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:30,950
Because the computer's operating system is actually stored on hard drive.

43
00:04:30,950 --> 00:04:38,350
And all the programs are initially placed in this hard drive or secondary storage itself.

44
00:04:38,350 --> 00:04:46,470
So the second example is, for example, you must also have access to the internet.

45
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:48,630
Everyone accesses the internet.

46
00:04:48,630 --> 00:04:56,510
So if a computer wants to access internet, it needs to use modem or network card.

47
00:04:56,510 --> 00:05:02,070
So modem is both input as well as output device because it sends the data as well as receives

48
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:03,070
the data.

49
00:05:03,070 --> 00:05:07,590
So modem is both input device as well as output device.

